    "question": "A 69-year-old male patient who was a cigarette smoker visited the doctor’s office complaining of a cough and congestion of the lungs. Routine cultures of early morning sputum for bacteria and AFB revealed no pathogens. A fungal culture grew the following on Sabouraud dextrose agar after 3 days: {{table}} What is the most likely identification?",
